>> # HOMIO / REOS — OIDC access-token verification
>>
>> This package provides a server-side verification boundary for signed JWT
>> access tokens. It does not own canonical identity records or tenant membership.
>>
>> ## Required runtime configuration
>>
>> Set these variables in the deployed service environment, never in source code:
>>
>> - `HOMIO_OIDC_ISSUER`: exact HTTPS issuer identifier expected in the token.
>> - `HOMIO_OIDC_AUDIENCE`: API/resource audience expected in the token.
>> - `HOMIO_OIDC_JWKS_URL`: trusted HTTPS URL publishing the issuer's signing keys.
>>
>> The verifier fails closed when any setting is missing or unsafe. Use the
>> issuer's official JWKS endpoint and configure the API's own audience.
>>
>> ## Use
>>
>> ```python
>> from AUTONOMY_ENGINE.security.authentication import OIDCSettings, OIDCVerifier
>>
>> settings = OIDCSettings.from_env()
>> verifier = OIDCVerifier(settings)
>> principal = verifier.verify_access_token(access_token)
>>
